    <dashboard name='Story 1' type='storyboard'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Book' fontsize='15'>This dataset contains biomechanical measurements from 310 patients used to classify spinal conditions. Patients are categorized into two groups: Normal and Abnormal. Abnormal cases include conditions such as disk hernia and spondylolisthesis. The distribution shows that abnormal cases make up a larger portion of the dataset, representing roughly two-thirds of all observations.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <style>
        <style-rule element='story-description'>
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_11' value='#00000000' />
          <format attr='border-width' id='story-description_11' value='0' />
          <format attr='border-style' id='story-description_11' value='none' />
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_12' value='#00000000' />
          <format attr='border-width' id='story-description_12' value='0' />
          <format attr='border-style' id='story-description_12' value='none' />
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_13' value='#00000000' />
          <format attr='border-width' id='story-description_13' value='0' />
          <format attr='border-style' id='story-description_13' value='none' />
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_14' value='#00000000' />
          <format attr='border-width' id='story-description_14' value='0' />
          <format attr='border-style' id='story-description_14' value='none' />
          <format attr='background-color' id='story-description_15' value='#00000000' />
          <format attr='border-width' id='story-description_15' value='0' />
          <format attr='border-style' id='story-description_15' value='none' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='story-point-caption'>
          <format attr='width' value='226' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size sizing-mode='automatic' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98352' id='9' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99034' x='483' y='824'>
            <zone h='11638' id='10' type-v2='title' w='99034' x='483' y='824'>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone h='86714' id='7' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99034' x='483' y='12462'>
              <zone h='86714' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99034' x='483' y='12462'>
                <zone h='10402' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='99034' x='483' y='12462' />
                <zone h='76312' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='99034' x='483' y='22864'>
                  <flipboard active-id='3' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                    <story-points>
                      <story-point caption='Data Overview' captured-sheet='Sheet 1' id='3' />
                      <story-point caption='Pelvic Incidence Differences Between Patient Groups' captured-sheet='Sheet 2' id='4' />
                      <story-point caption='Relationship Between Pelvic Incidence and Sacral Slope' captured-sheet='Sheet 3' id='5' />
                      <story-point caption='Distribution of Vertebral Displacement' captured-sheet='Sheet 4' id='6' />
                      <story-point caption='Key Findings' captured-sheet='' id='7' />
                    </story-points>
                  </flipboard>
                </zone>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='66220' id='11' story-point-id='3' type-v2='text' w='77791' x='17984' y='27806'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>This dataset contains biomechanical measurements from 310 patients used to classify spinal conditions. Patients are categorized into two groups: Normal and Abnormal. Abnormal cases include conditions such as disk hernia and spondylolisthesis. The distribution shows that abnormal cases make up a larger portion of the dataset, representing roughly two-thirds of all observations.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='46138' hidden='true' id='12' story-point-id='4' type-v2='text' w='74894' x='18709' y='36560'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Pelvic incidence is an important biomechanical parameter describing the orientation of the pelvis relative to the spine. The box plot shows that abnormal patients tend to have higher pelvic incidence values compared to normal patients. This suggests that pelvic alignment may play a role in spinal disorders.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='46344' hidden='true' id='13' story-point-id='5' type-v2='text' w='41521' x='46771' y='37693'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>The scatter plot reveals a strong positive relationship between pelvic incidence and sacral slope. As pelvic incidence increases, sacral slope also tends to increase. Abnormal patients appear more frequently in the higher measurement ranges, indicating that these biomechanical characteristics may be associated with spinal abnormalities.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='54377' hidden='true' id='14' story-point-id='6' type-v2='text' w='48582' x='40736' y='33059'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>The histogram of vertebral displacement (degree of spondylolisthesis) shows a clear difference between normal and abnormal patients. Normal cases cluster near zero displacement, while abnormal cases extend toward much higher values. This suggests that vertebral displacement is one of the strongest indicators of spinal disorders in this dataset.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='52626' hidden='true' id='15' story-point-id='7' type-v2='text' w='74170' x='13398' y='31514'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>The analysis highlights several biomechanical indicators associated with spinal abnormalities. Abnormal patients generally exhibit higher pelvic incidence values and greater vertebral displacement. A strong relationship between pelvic incidence and sacral slope was also observed. Among the variables analyzed, vertebral displacement appears to be the most distinctive indicator separating normal and abnormal spinal conditions.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{C8A330E2-AC42-4644-8DBF-537C0058943A}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
